# Stage 7b's criterion (TASK-24, docs/research/desktop/plan.md): the GUI
# test moves, minimises, restores and closes a terminal window over QMP,
# switches with Alt+Tab and F12, and passes at both scales. Coordinates
# are logical: the terminal's frame is at (72, 70), 670 wide, its title bar
# 36 high, the close cross at (90, 88) and the minimise dash at (114, 88)
# (ADR-0160; zoraya_compositor::ORIGIN under the 28-pixel bar).
serial init: gui: gpu on its own page
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
region 130 76 200 4 f7f7f8
region 72 120 1 300 d7d9de
shot windows-start
# Moved by its title bar, (100, 50) and back.
drag 300 88 400 138
region 230 126 200 4 f7f7f8
region 172 170 1 300 d7d9de
drag 400 138 300 88
region 130 76 200 4 f7f7f8
# Minimised by the dash; F12 brings it back, and it takes keys again.
click 114 88
key f12
type echo restored\r
screen restored
screen ~> _
# Minimised again; Alt+Tab (the switcher, chosen on Alt's release) brings
# it back.
click 114 88
chord alt tab
type echo switched\r
screen switched
screen ~> _
# Closed by the cross: the terminal ends, and init opens a new one with a
# new shell, as after exit.
click 90 88
serial init: the terminal was closed
window
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
# A new window takes focus only from the person (ADR-0094): its title bar,
# then its focused ground, before any key (on CI's slower runner the keys
# otherwise reached no window, 2026-11-09).
click 400 80
region 130 76 100 4 f7f7f8
# More clients than the compositor's 8 slots of before (proposed ADR-0323):
# nine terminals from the panel (System+Enter), eleven clients with this one
# and the chooser.
chord meta ret
pause 1500
chord meta ret
pause 1500
chord meta ret
pause 1500
chord meta ret
pause 1500
chord meta ret
pause 1500
chord meta ret
pause 1500
chord meta ret
pause 1500
chord meta ret
pause 1500
chord meta ret
# The tenth window is waited for, not a fixed time: under CI's TCG the
# terminals reach the compositor late ("term: waiting for the compositor"),
# and after 4 s only five windows were up, so the drag below took the fifth
# (cascaded 160 to the left) and the rows read at (361, 64) began mid-line
# with "or help tour." (2026-11-13). Each window is cascaded 32 to the
# right, the ninth of the panel's (n = 9) to the screen's right edge: its
# frame alone covers x 1004..1020 (the eighth's ends at 1000), so its body
# there is the tenth window, at both scales (1024 wide logically).
region 1004 300 16 100 ffffff
pause 1000
shot windows-many
# The tenth window, on top where the cascade meets the work area's corner,
# has its shell: it takes keys after a click on its title bar. With 8 slots
# the compositor refused the seventh of them. Where the cascade stops it
# depends on the terminal's height, which is not the same at both scales
# (its title bar is at y 196 at scale 1, 209 at scale 2), so it is first
# dragged by its title bar (y 220 is in it at both) up against the bar,
# where the compositor stops every window: its body then starts at
# (361, 64), the bar's 28 and the title bar's 36, at both scales.
# The drag moves it in steps, and the compositor draws each; under TCG a
# frame read after the release can still show it on the way, a row or more
# below its place, and a `screen` there matched the banner a row too low, so
# that the prompt, read later at its place, was above the match (CI,
# 2026-11-13). So the click that focuses it comes first: its input follows
# the release, and its focused title bar, waited for against the bar, is
# drawn only with the window at its place; then its rows are read.
drag 560 220 560 30
click 560 46
region 600 33 60 4 f7f7f8
origin 361 64
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
pause 500
type echo eleven clients\r
screen eleven clients
screen ~> _
# A terminal of the panel's has no power to end the machine: back to the
# first, init's, whose title bar shows above the others.
click 300 80
region 130 76 100 4 f7f7f8
# Keys typed at once after the focusing click can be lost under TCG (the
# first five of poweroff, locally and on CI); a hand is not that quick.
pause 500
type poweroff\r
exit
